    ],
    "reading_order": 10,
    "text": "The mean (or average) of observations, as we know, is the sum of the values of all the\nobservations divided by the total number of observations. From Class IX, recall that if\nx1, x2,. . ., xn are observations with respective frequencies f1, f2, . . ., fn, then this\nmeans observation x1 occurs f1 times, x2 occurs f2 times, and so on.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
